{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"Tiling time in 256-element chunks is a substantial win: it cuts the 4096-token case from about 38 µs to 29 µs and the 1024-token case from 35 µs to 27 µs. I’m adopting that geometry and trimming unnecessary FP64 work from `x1`; `x0` and `v` retain the high-accuracy path that protects the gated result."}}
