{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"The compiler strongly prefers keeping the three output stores together; forcing early stores reduced throughput, so I reverted that experiment. I’m now testing whether only the reduction—not the multiplications—needs FP64 precision. If rounded FP32 products still preserve the gated tolerance, this can remove the costliest double-precision instructions."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch,torch.nn.functional as F\nfor B,L in [(2,293),(1,512),(64,128),(32,256),(4,4096)]:\n torch.manual_seed(987+B+L);u=torch.randn((B,768,L),device='cuda');w=torch.randn((768,1,3),device='cuda');b=torch.randn(768,device='cuda');ref=F.conv1d(u,w,b,padding=2,groups=768)[...,:L]\n p=torch.cat((torch.zeros((B,768,2),device='cuda'),u),-1)\n ys={}\n y=b.double()[None,:,None]\n for k in range(3):y=y+(p[...,k:k+L]*w[:,0,k][None,:,None]).double()\n ys['fp32prod_fp64sum']=y.float()\n y=b[None,:,None]\n for k in range(3):y=y+p[...,k:k+L]*w[:,0,k][None,:,None]\n ys['fp32all']=y\n tol=dict(atol=1.969e-7,rtol=1.1920928955078125e-7)\n for name,y in ys.items():\n  g=y[:,512:]*y[:,:256];rg=ref[:,512:]*ref[:,:256]\n  rates=[torch.isclose(g,rg,**tol).float().mean(),torch.isclose(y[:,:256],ref[:,:256],**tol).float().mean(),torch.isclose(y[:,256:512],ref[:,256:512],**tol).float().mean()]\n  print(B,L,name,[round(x.item(),6) for x in rates],round(torch.stack(rates).mean().item(),6))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
